I like to have a reserve of stuff on hand for ascension run
emergencies.  I've noticed that the climb can go from "smooth sailing"
to "all hell breaks loose and you're fuckered" very very rapidly.  I
like to keep an (oilskin) sack with stuff I might need right now in
addition to the bag of holding (stuff I might need, but not on a
moment's notice, goes in here).

A fairly minimal (oilskin) sack inventory:

2x scrolls of remove curse
2x scrolls of blank paper
1x potion of holy water
1x potion of full healing
rings of conflict, free action, telecontrol, teleport, levitation
1x wand of death <-- Orcus', usually.
1x wand of wishing <-- Castle, preferably (1:3), minimum (1:1)
1x wand of cancellation <-- all named "CAUTION, MAGIC BAG GO BOOM!"
2x wand of teleprotation <-- the more the merrier
1x wand of secret door detection <-- emerg. portal detection
1x uncursed magic marker (1:50) <-- emergency use only
1x Bag of Holding <-- all my other crap goes in here.  It can't be
cursed if it's inside another container.

If the Bag of Holding goes poof in a nasty accident, there's the bare
minimum in the (oilskin) sack to get me through the planes to astral.

